static char *translate_digimax(char *progname, char *sunchanged, char *launchp)
{
 return "\n"
  "usage: %s <seed> [dump]\n"
  "\n"
  "  seed:   random number seed\n"
  "  dump:   dump out the state of the PRNG after each step\n"
  "\n"
  "This program tests the PRNG used by the kernel's random number\n"
  "generator. It takes one argument, which is the seed to use.\n"
  "If a second argument is given, then the state of the PRNG will\n"
  "be dumped out after each step.\n"
  "\n"
  "The output consists of a sequence of numbers, each of which is\n"
  "a random number generated by the kernel's PRNG. If the PRNG is\n"
  "working correctly, these numbers should be uniformly distributed\n"
  "over the range of possible values.\n"
  "\n"
  "If the PRNG is broken, then the sequence of numbers will either\n"
  "repeat (in which case the program will terminate) or fail the\n"
  "statistical tests for randomness (in which case the program will\n"
  "print an error message).\n"
  "\n"
  "If the PRNG is working correctly, then the sequence of numbers\n"
  "will appear to be random, and will not repeat.\n"
  "\n"
  "The PRNG is implemented using a cryptographically secure hash\n"
  "function, so if it is broken, then the entire system is\n"
  "potentially insecure.\n"
  "\n"
  "For more information, see the man page for this program.\n"
  "\n";
}